     1	# Curator Protocol Core 1.0
     2	
     3	This document is normative. It defines the portable objects and deterministic
     4	algorithms shared by conforming Curator Protocol managers. Tool-specific state
     5	and user interfaces are defined outside the core.
     6	
     7	## 1. Data model and versioning
     8	
     9	Protocol JSON MUST be UTF-8 without a byte-order mark. Parsers MUST reject
    10	duplicate object keys, invalid UTF-8, trailing non-whitespace data, and values
    11	that violate the applicable schema under `../schemas/v1/`.
    12	
    13	JSON object member order and insignificant whitespace have no meaning unless a
    14	section explicitly defines canonical bytes. Array order is significant unless
    15	the field is declared set-like. Writers MUST emit the current schema version;
    16	readers MUST reject unsupported versions with an upgrade error and MUST NOT
    17	infer a newer schema from its fields.
    18	
    19	Schemas define structural validity. The semantic checks in this document are
    20	additional and REQUIRED.
    21	
    22	### 1.1 Compatibility identifiers
    23	
    24	The filenames `Skillfile.json`, `Skillfile.dev.json`, `agent-skill.json`,
    25	`.csk-install.json`, `.csk-managed.json`, and project root `.agents/` are
    26	portable protocol identifiers. A manager MUST read and write those exact names.
    27	The filename `csk-skill.json` is a reserved legacy alias for
    28	`agent-skill.json`: managers MUST continue to read it throughout protocol 1.x,
    29	but writers MUST emit only `agent-skill.json`.
    30	
    31	Machine-home directories, cache names, executable names, global environment
    32	variables, and managed comment text are implementation-specific. A manager
    33	MUST NOT write machine-local state into another manager's home unless the user
    34	explicitly selected that location.
    35	
    36	## 2. Portable identifiers and paths
    37	
    38	Skill names, command names, MCP server names, agent identifiers, and adapter
    39	ledger entries MUST match:
    40	
    41	```text
    42	^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]*$
    43	```
    44	
    45	They MUST additionally satisfy the portable filename rules below. Comparison
    46	is case-sensitive even on a case-insensitive filesystem.
    47	
    48	A portable relative path:
    49	
    50	1. is a non-empty Unicode string encoded as UTF-8;
    51	2. uses `/` separators and contains no `\`, NUL, or control character;
    52	3. is not absolute and has no empty, `.` or `..` component;
    53	4. has no component ending in a space or `.` and no component containing `:`;
    54	5. has no component whose case-insensitive basename before its first `.` is
    55	   `CON`, `PRN`, `AUX`, `NUL`, `COM1` through `COM9`, or `LPT1` through `LPT9`.
    56	
    57	Implementations MUST preserve Unicode scalar values exactly and MUST NOT apply
    58	normalization during hashing or comparison. Filesystem extraction MUST detect
    59	two protocol paths that map to one platform path and fail before writing.
    60	
    61	## 3. Skill packages
    62	
    63	A skill package is a git snapshot or a directory within one. Its root MUST
    64	contain `SKILL.md` with YAML frontmatter containing non-empty `name` and
    65	`description` strings. The frontmatter `name` MUST equal the declared skill
    66	name. `triggers`, when present, is a list of non-empty strings.
    67	
    68	An installer MUST NOT execute package-provided code while resolving,
    69	validating, auditing, or installing a skill.
    70	
    71	### 3.1 Context selection
    72	
    73	Only these root entries are eligible for agent-facing context:
    74	
    75	```text
    76	SKILL.md
    77	agents/
    78	references/
    79	.skill_triggers/
    80	assets/
    81	templates/
    82	examples/
    83	data/
    84	```
    85	
    86	`scripts/` is additionally eligible only when the package exports no commands.
    87	At every depth the following names or glob patterns MUST be excluded:
    88	
    89	```text
    90	.git .github .gitlab-ci.yml .venv __pycache__ *.pyc node_modules
    91	tests test __tests__ README* CHANGELOG* LICENSE* Makefile
    92	setup.py pyproject.toml requirements*.txt .DS_Store .gitignore
    93	```
    94	
    95	Directories declared in `runtime_roots` are excluded even if nested under an
    96	eligible context root. Selection uses protocol paths, sorts selected files by
    97	Unicode scalar value of their POSIX path, rejects links, and copies regular
    98	file bytes without newline conversion.
    99	
   100	### 3.2 Localization
   101	
   102	Localization is inactive when no locale is selected. When
   103	`locales/metadata.json` exists it MUST contain an object `locales`; when
   104	`.skill_triggers/` exists it MUST be a directory. A consistent locale has both
   105	`locales[locale]` and `.skill_triggers/<locale>.md`. At least one consistent
   106	locale is REQUIRED when either localization surface exists.
   107	
   108	A locale selector is 1 through 64 ASCII letters, digits, or hyphens, starts and
   109	ends with a letter or digit, and is compared case-sensitively without
   110	normalization. Every `locales` member name MUST be a locale selector and its
   111	value MUST be an object. This deliberately uses a safe BCP 47-compatible
   112	surface without attempting language-tag canonicalization.
   113	
   114	For a selected consistent locale, a manager replaces only the `description`
   115	and `triggers` values in installed `SKILL.md`, preserving `name` and body. List
   116	items beginning with `- ` outside fenced code blocks form the trigger list.
   117	When present, `agents/openai.yaml` is rendered from `display_name`,
   118	`short_description`, and `default_prompt`. If the selected locale is
   119	unavailable, source context is installed unchanged and a warning lists the
   120	available consistent locales. The warning is emitted even for an otherwise
   121	current installation.
   122	
   123	## 4. Skill manifest
   124	
   125	`agent-skill.json` is OPTIONAL for a pure context skill and otherwise conforms
   126	to exactly one of `agent-skill-v1.schema.json` through
   127	`agent-skill-v5.schema.json`. The legacy filename `csk-skill.json` has exactly
   128	the same object shape; its unchanged `csk-skill-v1.schema.json` through
   129	`csk-skill-v5.schema.json` series remains the compatibility contract.
   130	
   131	Readers resolve manifests in this order:
   132	
   133	1. When only `agent-skill.json` exists, read it.
   134	2. When only `csk-skill.json` exists, read it as a legacy manifest.
   135	3. When both exist, parse and validate both independently. They MUST represent
   136	   equal JSON values: object member order and insignificant whitespace are
   137	   ignored, array order and JSON value types remain significant. If equal,
   138	   `agent-skill.json` is authoritative. If unequal, the reader MUST fail with
   139	   `conflicting_skill_manifests` and MUST NOT install either value.
   140	4. The existence of an invalid modern manifest is an error and MUST NOT fall
   141	   back to the other filename or to `agents/runtime.json`.
   142	
   143	| Schema | Added behavior |
   144	|---|---|
   145	| 1 | exported script and system commands |
   146	| 2 | `runtime_roots`, command dependencies, strict top-level fields |
   147	| 3 | REQUIRED capability declaration |
   148	| 4 | transitive skill requirements |
   149	| 5 | MCP server requirements |
   150	
   151	Version gates are downward: a field introduced by a later version MUST be
   152	rejected in an earlier one. Schema 1 preserves its deployed extension behavior;
   153	schemas 2 through 5 reject unknown fields.
   154	
   155	### 4.1 Runtime roots and commands
   156	
   157	Every runtime root and script command path MUST be a portable relative path
   158	that exists in the snapshot. Runtime roots MUST name directories, be unique,
   159	and be pairwise disjoint. For schema 2 and later, every script command path
   160	MUST fall within one declared runtime root when any roots are declared.
   161	
   162	A script command declares at least one of `unix_path` and `win_path`. A system
   163	command declares a non-empty bare executable name and MAY include a hint. A
   164	missing system command fails installation with the hint. The command name is
   165	the shim name and one active name has exactly one owner.
   166	
   167	### 4.2 Capabilities
   168	
   169	Schema 3 and later require `capabilities`. Capabilities are an audit surface,
   170	not a runtime sandbox:
   171	
   172	- `network`: `"none"` or unique host globs without whitespace or path syntax;
   173	- `filesystem`: `"repo"`, `"home-config"`, or unique portable paths;
   174	- `exec`: `"none"` or unique bare executable names;
   175	- `secrets`: `"none"` or unique non-empty secret identifiers;
   176	- `env_read`: unique environment-variable names;
   177	- `prompt_scope`: an OPTIONAL non-empty purpose statement.
   178	
   179	Missing OPTIONAL capability fields take their schema defaults.
   180	

