497:<p>For developers familiar with <code>npm link</code> in Node.js, Deno provides a similar
498:feature for local JSR and npm packages through the <code>links</code> field in <code>deno.json</code>.
529:<li>Both JSR and npm packages are supported.</li>
538:<h3 id="overriding-npm-packages" tabindex="-1">Overriding NPM packages <a class="header-anchor" href="#overriding-npm-packages"><span class="sr-only">Jump to heading</span><span aria-hidden="true" class="anchor-end">#</span></a></h3>
539:<p>Deno supports linking npm packages with local versions, similar to how JSR
540:packages can be linked. This allows you to use a local copy of an npm package
542:<p>To use a local npm package, configure the <code>links</code> field in your <code>deno.json</code>:</p>
545:    <span class="token string">"../path/to/local_npm_package"</span>
552:    &quot;../path/to/local_npm_package&quot;
